### Edit 2 🔴 (finding 34 + new) — hosting-modes table misdescribes "Dedicated"

The current table implies a dedicated Azure environment per Dedicated customer. In production, `terraform/environments/app-production/workloads/main.tf` instantiates every tenant through the same `module "customer_tenant" { for_each = local.tenants }`, all sharing one AKS cluster, one PostgreSQL Flexible Server, one Key Vault, and one ACR. Dedicated mode is logical (namespace + database + storage container + secret prefix), not environmental.

**Current**

| Mode | Description |
|---|---|
| Shared (Normain-managed) | Customer tenant in Normain's shared Microsoft Azure environment. |
| Dedicated (Normain-managed) | Customer tenant in a dedicated Microsoft Azure environment operated by Normain. |
| Customer-hosted | Deployment in a cloud environment provided by the Customer. |

**Proposed**

| Mode | Description |
|---|---|
| **Shared (Normain-managed)** | Customer organisation provisioned within Normain's multi-tenant `app.normain.com` tenant in Normain's shared Microsoft Azure environment. |
| **Dedicated tenant (Normain-managed)** | Customer receives a dedicated subdomain, Kubernetes namespace, PostgreSQL database, storage container, and Entra tenant integration within Normain's shared Microsoft Azure environment (shared AKS cluster, PostgreSQL server, and Key Vault). |
| **Customer-hosted (Microsoft Azure)** | Deployment in a customer-provided Microsoft Azure environment operated by the Customer using Normain-published Terraform modules. |

Add a scoping sentence directly under the table:

> During the examination period (4 May – 4 Aug 2026), all customers operate under Shared or Dedicated tenant modes. No customer operates under Customer-hosted mode.

(Confirm before issuance — if a Customer-hosted customer exists, scope changes.)

