## DC 3.6 — Operational Access — No Customer Production Data

### Edit 6 ⚠️ (new) — missing operational third parties

Three operationally-used third parties are not listed and process either billing PII or end-user contact data:

- **Stripe** — billing PII (org email, payment method). `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` + `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` in production IaC; `Stripe` SDK in `src/shared/payments`.
- **Loops** — transactional/marketing email to end-user addresses. `LOOPS_API_KEY` in production IaC; `loops` SDK in `src/apps/server/api/src/utils/auth/client/loopsContact.ts`.
- **Zero** — sales-lead webhook (signup notifications). `ZERO_WEBHOOK_URL = https://api.zero.inc/...` in production env vars; called from `src/apps/server/api/src/utils/auth/client/notifyLeadsWebhook.ts`.

**Add rows** to the existing DC 3.6 table:

| Vendor | Role |
|---|---|
| Stripe | Subscription billing and payment processing (self-serve customers). |
| Loops | Transactional and marketing email delivery. |
| Zero | Sales-lead notification webhook. |

(Confirm with Legal whether Loops and Zero belong in DC 3.5 instead, depending on whether end-user email is treated as customer-content.)

